    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d425">

                <pb facs="0543" n="475" sameAs="frus:frus1914-20v01/pg475"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">841.857/32½</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">President Wilson to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-09-07">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">7 September, 1915</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: The sinking of the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Hesperian</hi><anchor n="49a" xml:id="d425-f1"/> has for
                    the time arrested everything, and therefore an answer to the enclosed<anchor
                        n="50" xml:id="d425-f2"/> is perhaps too much belated to be of any use to
                    you. But this is clear, that we should let the German Government know that it
                    was not wise to wait too long to state their attitude and the course they intend
                    to pursue with regard to the sinking of the <hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Arabic</hi>.</p>
                <p>However, we shall not be certain of anything until we hear all the facts about
                    the <hi rendition="#italic">Hesperian</hi>.</p>
                <p>Faithfully Yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>W. W.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d425-f1" n="49a" xml:id="d425-f1-content">
                <p>For correspondence previously printed regarding the <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Hesperian</hi>, see <ref target="frus1915Supp#pg_533">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">ibid.</hi>, pp. 533</ref>–<ref
                        target="frus1915Supp#pg_556">556</ref>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">passim</hi>, and <ref target="frus1915Supp#pg_607">p.
                        607</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d425-f2" n="50" xml:id="d425-f2-content">
                <p>Nose of Sept. 3, 1915, from the German Ambassador, <ref
                        target="frus1915Supp#pg_533">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">ibid.</hi>, 533</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
